; Leg CD -- the host RECEIVES.  The Victor SENDS TRANS.DAT with PX_ALL.
;
; THE CONTROL FOR LEG CC, and it is an unusually good one: CKPXALL.EXE is
; built from the same tree, the same commit and the same flags as
; CKERMITW.EXE, differing only in the immediate constant the prefixing
; initializer stores.  Both are 205,228 bytes.  wdis shows the whole
; difference:
;
;     CKERMITW  mov word ptr _ptab+0cH,1        ; PX_CAU
;     CKPXALL   xor ax,ax / mov ..., ax         ; PX_ALL
;
; So SS16w's finding that this machine is sensitive to code size has NO
; purchase here -- the layouts are identical.  That is worth having,
; because SS16af had to spend a whole null leg establishing the same thing
; for a change that did alter code size.
;
; NOTE THE DIRECTION.  Host receives, so START THIS FIRST.
;
; It should reproduce SS16ah leg BS, which ran a DIFFERENT binary (205,256,
; md5 433148fa, pre-edit-17-era numbering) but the same effective policy:
;
;     prefixing policy   PX_ALL exactly (66 values)
;     prefixes  ctl      8,869
;     WIRE BYTES         41,945
;
; A CD that does NOT reproduce BS's prefix count means something other than
; prefixing moved between the two binaries, and CC is then not attributable
; either.  That is the null-leg discipline of SS16af: spend a leg on the
; result that is supposed to be nothing.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16aiCD.pkt
receive gotcd.dat
statistics
